      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EMPIRE RULER (4) has the clearest winning case after four straight placings, including a Gawler second when beaten just over half a length by Miami Miller. The new 2050m task is the one reservation, but first-time blinkers and his reliable recent form have him on top. Deserves the win and should go close. RICH MELODY (6) is the main danger after consecutive thirds at Gawler, the latest beaten just under a length, and he is close enough to EMPIRE RULER on that recent meeting to keep pressure on the top pick. CHILLY BRO (3) was plain on paper last start, but he covered ground and had a bumping incident after a near-miss at Murray Bridge. In the mix. LADY DEEDS (9) was sound first-up at Gawler and her narrow second at this track before the break gives her a genuine place chance if she begins cleanly.",
